# NTLinux Phase 0 archiso package list.
#
# Base: mirrors the upstream archiso `releng` profile's live-boot essentials
# (not reproduced verbatim here — before building, diff this file against
# https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/archiso releng/packages.x86_64 and
# merge in whatever live-boot packages that profile carries at build time;
# distro kernels/tooling move fast enough that pinning them here would rot).
#
# Everything below "NTLinux Phase 0 stack" is what this project adds, grouped
# by docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section. See distro/packages/base.list for the
# same list with per-line rationale.

# --- archiso live-boot essentials (subset; diff against releng) ---
base
base-devel
linux
linux-firmware
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
syslinux
grub
efibootmgr
networkmanager
sudo
nano
vim
git

# --- NTLinux Phase 0 stack ---
# Scope note: KVM/VFIO/libvirt packages are deliberately NOT here. Phase 0
# is the baseline gaming distro (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 43); the
# ReactOS driver cell and its KVM/VFIO dependencies are Phase 4+
# (ROADMAP.md). Keep this list matched to the Phase 0 "Deliver" list only.

# Kernel-side NT sync (section 1.2, 53.3): ntsync is mainline in `linux`
# since 6.14, no separate package needed — see kernel/config/ for the
# config fragment that confirms it's enabled.

# Graphics: Mesa + Vulkan (section 30)
mesa
vulkan-icd-loader
vulkan-radeon
vulkan-intel
lib32-mesa
lib32-vulkan-icd-loader
lib32-vulkan-radeon
lib32-vulkan-intel

# Display/session (section 9) — Wayland compositor stack.
# plasma-desktop (not the plasma-meta metapackage) + a terminal and file
# manager: the shell/desktop-mode session, not the full KDE app suite
# (Kontact, Elisa, etc. add ~160 more packages for no Phase-0 benefit).
wayland
xorg-xwayland
plasma-desktop
dolphin
konsole
sddm
gamescope

# Audio (section 31)
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-jack
wireplumber

# Input (section 32): no separate package — Steam's own package installs
# udev rules covering most controllers (60-steam-input.rules etc.); the
# `game-devices-udev` package some distro wikis reference is AUR-only, not
# in the official repos, so it's intentionally not listed here.

# Windows compatibility layer (section 3, 10, 38)
wine
wine-staging
winetricks
steam
gamemode
lib32-gamemode

# --- NTLinux Phase 1 additions (native Windows executable UX) ---
# python: runs tooling/installer/ntlinux-app (already pulled in transitively
# by several packages above, listed explicitly since Phase 1 now depends on
# it directly, not just incidentally).
# icoutils: wrestool/icotool, used by ntlinux-app to extract a real desktop
# icon from a PE binary's own resources (Rule 1: reuse, don't hand-parse
# ICO/PE resource sections).
python
icoutils

# graphics/dxvk, graphics/vkd3d-proton note (ADR-0002: consume, don't vendor):
# Steam's own Proton already bundles matching DXVK/vkd3d-proton builds, so
# no separate package is required for Proton games out of the box. For
# non-Steam Wine prefixes, dxvk-bin/vkd3d-proton are AUR packages, not in
# the official repos — an archiso build needs either (a) a local/
# Chaotic-AUR-style package repo baked into pacman.conf, or (b) to leave
# them to the user's package manager post-boot. Phase 0 ships without them
# pre-baked; tracked as a Phase 0 follow-up in ROADMAP.md.
